From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] cuda: route sm_121 to the Turing mmvq parameter table

First of the three patches that together carry the sm_121 wide Q4_K mmvq
vec_dot to this track (0003 table alias, 0004 dedicated SM121 table, 0005
the wide vec_dot itself). They are measured as one unit here - see 0005's
message and the README for this track's numbers - because 0005 cannot exist
without the SM121 table id that 0003/0004 introduce.

GB10 decode measures the MoE expert matvecs well below achievable bandwidth
under the GENERIC mmvq config (4 warps/row): the LPDDR5 latency wants more
ILP per warp, not more warps. The Turing table (2 warps for K-quants) is the
right shape. Verified separately on the qwen3.6 and laguna-xs GB10 twins,
which share Laguna S's 256-expert top-8 routing.
---
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu
index c3f95f9..abea72f 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu
@@ -83,6 +83,11 @@ static constexpr __device__ mmvq_parameter_table_id get_device_table_id() {
     return MMVQ_PARAMETERS_GCN;
 #elif defined(__CUDA_ARCH__) && __CUDA_ARCH__ >= GGML_CUDA_CC_TURING && __CUDA_ARCH__ < GGML_CUDA_CC_AMPERE
     return MMVQ_PARAMETERS_TURING;
+#elif defined(__CUDA_ARCH__) && __CUDA_ARCH__ == 1210
+    // GB10 (sm_121): LPDDR5 latency-bound decode measures the MoE expert
+    // matvecs at 35-40% of achievable bandwidth under the GENERIC config;
+    // the Turing table (2 warps for K-quants) trades warp count for ILP.
+    return MMVQ_PARAMETERS_TURING;
 #else
     return MMVQ_PARAMETERS_GENERIC;
 #endif
@@ -104,6 +109,9 @@ static __host__ mmvq_parameter_table_id get_device_table_id(int cc) {
     if (GGML_CUDA_CC_IS_NVIDIA(cc) && ggml_cuda_highest_compiled_arch(cc) >= GGML_CUDA_CC_TURING && ggml_cuda_highest_compiled_arch(cc) < GGML_CUDA_CC_AMPERE) {
         return MMVQ_PARAMETERS_TURING;
     }
+    if (GGML_CUDA_CC_IS_NVIDIA(cc) && ggml_cuda_highest_compiled_arch(cc) == 1210) {
+        return MMVQ_PARAMETERS_TURING;
+    }
     return MMVQ_PARAMETERS_GENERIC;
 }
 
